    statement: "Organizers that encrypt users' messages, or let users encrypt them, must give the FSB the information needed to decode them. The same article requires messengers to keep messages confidential.",
    analysis: "Art. 10.1(4.1) applies when the service offers users the ability to encode messages. In E2EE the session keys are generated and held on endpoints. The organizer has no decoding information to hand over unless it redesigns to capture keys, which is key escrow. Art. 10.1(4.2)(4) in the same article requires instant-messaging organizers to ensure message confidentiality. A service can meet 4.1 only by holding keys, and holding keys makes every message readable by the organizer and anyone who compromises it.",
